# OpenSpec + Superpowers (Cursor)

Requires **Superpowers plugin**: `/add-plugin superpowers`. Full setup: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/superpowers/README.md`.

## Slash commands

| Command | Use when |
|---------|----------|
| `/opsx-propose` | New change — full artifact set (superpowers-bridge default) |
| `/opsx-new` | Scaffold change only |
| `/opsx-continue` | Next artifact in the change |
| `/opsx-ff` | Fast-forward all planning artifacts |
| `/opsx-explore` | Think only — no product code |
| `/opsx-apply` | Implement (worktree + subagents + TDD when using superpowers-bridge) |
| `/opsx-verify` | Post-apply verification artifact |
| `/opsx-sync` | Sync delta specs to main specs |
| `/opsx-archive` | Archive completed change |

## Schema routing

- **Default:** `superpowers-bridge` (`openspec/config.yaml`)
- **bootstrap-local-platform:** stays `spec-driven` — use `/opsx-apply bootstrap-local-platform`
- **Trivial fix (bug/typo/docs):** direct PR, no opsx change

## Superpowers skills (auto via plugin)

Before implementation: brainstorming → writing-plans → using-git-worktrees → subagent-driven-development (includes TDD + code review). Do not write brainstorm/plan output to `docs/superpowers/` for active changes — use `openspec/changes/<name>/`.

## Verbal brainstorm

If user brainstorms in chat without `/opsx:*`, do not write to `docs/superpowers/specs/`. When scope + forks + deps + acceptance + convergence are clear, suggest `/opsx-propose` and wait for ack.
